1
00:00:47,075 --> 00:00:50,466
Throughout film history,
behind every great filmmaker...

2
00:00:50,466 --> 00:00:54,626
[Lost Time]
There was a great muse who inspired them.

3
00:00:54,626 --> 00:00:55,490
[Director Yang Bursts Onto the Scene]

4
00:00:55,490 --> 00:00:57,456
[Director Yang Jun Mo Wins Best Director]

5
00:00:58,271 --> 00:01:01,142
But here's the irony.

6
00:01:01,142 --> 00:01:03,159
When that muse leaves,

7
00:01:03,159 --> 00:01:06,252
what becomes of the creator left behind?

8
00:01:07,739 --> 00:01:11,096
Of course, every case is different.

9
00:01:13,652 --> 00:01:17,489
Some are branded as masters in name only,

10
00:01:17,489 --> 00:01:21,049
unable to prove anything on their own.

11
00:01:22,530 --> 00:01:24,461
Today on Cool Guy's Take,

12
00:01:24,461 --> 00:01:27,164
we're joined by film critic Hong Jae Hui

13
00:01:27,164 --> 00:01:30,890
to talk about great filmmakers and their muses.

14
00:01:37,097 --> 00:01:38,643
[Episode 9]

15
00:01:39,852 --> 00:01:42,958
- Looking forward to it.
- Likewise.

16
00:01:43,962 --> 00:01:45,615
- Shall we?
- Let's go.

17
00:01:47,182 --> 00:01:48,879
How'd the interview go?

18
00:01:48,879 --> 00:01:50,299
Good.

19
00:01:52,932 --> 00:01:55,830
You looking for something?

20
00:01:55,830 --> 00:01:56,874
Where's Yoon Ha Na?

21
00:01:56,874 --> 00:01:58,196
What?

22
00:02:00,045 --> 00:02:04,434
I saw her heading that way with Ha Ru earlier.

23
00:02:04,434 --> 00:02:05,819
Okay.

24
00:02:15,330 --> 00:02:19,990
So Eun Soo is you, and Yeong Hyeon is Woo Jae.

25
00:02:20,740 --> 00:02:22,620
So...

26
00:02:22,620 --> 00:02:26,786
They keep traveling through time
with the camcorder...

27
00:02:26,786 --> 00:02:28,663
to save the male lead.

28
00:02:28,663 --> 00:02:32,795
Everything that happened
to Woo Jae and me is in here.

29
00:02:33,571 --> 00:02:35,851
Like someone was watching us the whole time.

30
00:02:37,816 --> 00:02:39,595
But from here...

31
00:02:40,276 --> 00:02:44,347
This is after we came back
to the future, right?

32
00:02:44,347 --> 00:02:45,917
Yeah.

33
00:02:45,917 --> 00:02:49,817
The us we don't remember.

34
00:02:51,496 --> 00:02:54,626
Even the part where Woo Jae and I broke up...

35
00:02:54,626 --> 00:02:56,352
It's all in here.

36
00:03:16,418 --> 00:03:18,262
I'm doing that movie.

37
00:03:18,262 --> 00:03:20,042
Don't try to stop me.

38
00:03:22,553 --> 00:03:25,393
This is a huge opportunity for me.

39
00:03:26,373 --> 00:03:29,297
Eun Soo, you'll get other chances.

40
00:03:29,297 --> 00:03:30,534
It doesn't have to be this...

41
00:03:30,534 --> 00:03:33,213
Why are you so against it?

42
00:03:33,213 --> 00:03:35,457
Everyone else is happy for me. Why are you...

43
00:03:35,457 --> 00:03:37,343
Director Cha Seo Yeon.

44
00:03:39,900 --> 00:03:42,919
I don't like you being around him.

45
00:03:42,919 --> 00:03:44,205
This again?

46
00:03:44,205 --> 00:03:46,249
The only reason he's being nice to you

47
00:03:46,249 --> 00:03:48,533
is because he wants something.

48
00:03:48,533 --> 00:03:50,139
Hey, Choi Yeong Hyeon.

49
00:03:50,139 --> 00:03:52,290
You can dislike someone.

50
00:03:52,290 --> 00:03:54,801
You don't even need a reason.

51
00:03:54,801 --> 00:03:59,556
But you, of all people,
shouldn't treat him like that.

52
00:03:59,556 --> 00:04:00,459
What?

53
00:04:00,459 --> 00:04:02,497
Honestly, you owe where you are now

54
00:04:02,497 --> 00:04:05,035
to that short film you made with him.

55
00:04:05,035 --> 00:04:08,412
And you'd accuse him on a hunch?

56
00:04:10,879 --> 00:04:13,336
I'm not saying this for no reason...

57
00:04:13,336 --> 00:04:16,401
I've known him longer than you have.
I know him better.

58
00:04:17,067 --> 00:04:19,367
He's not like that.

59
00:04:19,367 --> 00:04:21,451
And more than anything...

60
00:04:21,451 --> 00:04:25,444
he's the only one who believes in me right now.

61
00:04:25,444 --> 00:04:28,051
I know you don't like him.

62
00:04:28,051 --> 00:04:31,758
But I'm doing this movie.

63
00:04:31,758 --> 00:04:35,404
I really want to make it work.

64
00:04:37,918 --> 00:04:43,206
Nothing I say gets through to you.

65
00:04:43,206 --> 00:04:44,292
Yeong Hyeon.

66
00:04:44,292 --> 00:04:46,464
If you're going to do his movie...

67
00:04:48,517 --> 00:04:50,522
then break up with me first.

68
00:04:52,311 --> 00:04:53,751
What?

69
00:05:29,291 --> 00:05:31,999
Do you think Woo Jae and I really...

70
00:05:31,999 --> 00:05:34,242
broke up like this?

71
00:05:35,599 --> 00:05:39,319
He begged me not to do it...

72
00:05:39,319 --> 00:05:42,666
and I just ignored him?

73
00:05:42,666 --> 00:05:44,932
We don't know that yet.

74
00:05:44,932 --> 00:05:47,972
This could just be a story
that Chu Si Hwan made up.

75
00:05:51,549 --> 00:05:53,174
And whoever wrote this...

76
00:05:53,174 --> 00:05:56,299
how does he know everything
you two said in private?

77
00:05:56,299 --> 00:05:58,402
Was he bugging you or something?

78
00:05:58,402 --> 00:06:00,663
We need to find this bastard.

79
00:06:00,663 --> 00:06:05,125
Let's figure out who he is,
then go back to 2017.

80
00:06:05,125 --> 00:06:09,279
I won't let Woo Jae get hurt again.

81
00:06:09,279 --> 00:06:11,752
I'll protect him this time.

82
00:06:11,752 --> 00:06:14,098
- Yeah.
- Protect who?

83
00:06:20,450 --> 00:06:22,582
[Lost Time]

84
00:06:34,626 --> 00:06:36,572
Record it...

85
00:06:43,009 --> 00:06:44,915
Then it gets saved...

86
00:06:46,855 --> 00:06:49,555
And if I travel to the time it was saved...

87
00:06:53,413 --> 00:06:54,985
How?

88
00:07:00,212 --> 00:07:01,542
What are you doing?

89
00:07:01,542 --> 00:07:02,883
If I do this...

90
00:07:02,883 --> 00:07:04,469
I should go back to the time I came from...

91
00:07:04,469 --> 00:07:07,255
Hey, what the hell are you doing?

92
00:07:18,068 --> 00:07:19,219
Cut.

93
00:07:19,219 --> 00:07:20,274
What?

94
00:07:20,274 --> 00:07:21,760
I said cut.

95
00:07:22,941 --> 00:07:27,546
I never gave you any lines,
so keep your mouth shut.

96
00:07:29,741 --> 00:07:31,290
Drive.

97
00:07:31,290 --> 00:07:34,272
There's no scene where you die
in a car crash today.

98
00:07:43,219 --> 00:07:46,084
Did you read the whole script?

99
00:07:47,818 --> 00:07:49,649
Oh, yeah.

100
00:07:49,649 --> 00:07:51,175
I did.

101
00:07:52,091 --> 00:07:54,989
Take out the time-travel fantasy
and change the year...

102
00:07:54,989 --> 00:07:58,915
and it's basically our story.

103
00:08:01,025 --> 00:08:02,588
Yeah.

104
00:08:02,588 --> 00:08:04,609
Darn it.

105
00:08:04,609 --> 00:08:06,242
I can't slip up...

106
00:08:06,242 --> 00:08:07,520
Exactly.

107
00:08:07,520 --> 00:08:10,499
A camcorder that travels through time?

108
00:08:10,499 --> 00:08:11,623
It's not a time machine.

109
00:08:11,623 --> 00:08:13,939
That's ridiculous, right?

110
00:08:13,939 --> 00:08:16,605
That's all you have to say?

111
00:08:19,296 --> 00:08:20,662
No, I mean...

112
00:08:20,662 --> 00:08:23,319
I was shocked too because it's our story.

113
00:08:23,319 --> 00:08:25,019
Whoever the bastard...

114
00:08:26,132 --> 00:08:28,217
I mean, whoever the director is...

115
00:08:28,217 --> 00:08:30,102
how would they even know about us?

116
00:08:30,709 --> 00:08:32,137
Right?

117
00:08:33,362 --> 00:08:36,682
You don't know who the director is?

118
00:08:39,585 --> 00:08:41,057
Don't tell me...

119
00:08:42,012 --> 00:08:43,812
It's Lee Hyeong Won, right?

120
00:08:44,632 --> 00:08:46,218
What?

121
00:08:46,218 --> 00:08:47,679
Why?

122
00:08:47,679 --> 00:08:50,731
It's not him?

123
00:08:53,011 --> 00:08:54,576
What are you doing? Let go!

124
00:08:54,576 --> 00:08:56,759
We'll check the school's CCTV.

125
00:08:56,759 --> 00:08:58,784
You may not believe me,
but you'll believe that.

126
00:08:58,784 --> 00:09:00,269
Let go of me first.

127
00:09:00,269 --> 00:09:03,268
You know how worried you made me?

128
00:09:05,270 --> 00:09:06,729
Sorry?

129
00:09:06,729 --> 00:09:08,502
Look at me too.

130
00:09:09,704 --> 00:09:11,633
Not just Jung Woo Jae.

131
00:09:15,925 --> 00:09:17,851
Lee Hyeong Won!

132
00:09:23,907 --> 00:09:25,230
I like you.

133
00:09:25,230 --> 00:09:30,174
I like you, Jung Woo Jae.

134
00:09:51,791 --> 00:09:53,374
Come with me.

135
00:11:05,308 --> 00:11:07,864
You're friends with Hyeong Won?

136
00:11:07,864 --> 00:11:09,009
Are you two close?

137
00:11:09,009 --> 00:11:11,509
How much do you trust that guy?

138
00:11:11,509 --> 00:11:12,952
What are you doing right now?

139
00:11:12,952 --> 00:11:15,345
You know he disappeared, right?

140
00:11:15,345 --> 00:11:18,498
That's suspicious.
He has no reason to disappear.

141
00:11:22,137 --> 00:11:23,752
"I've always...

142
00:11:24,434 --> 00:11:27,375
wanted a new white outfit."

143
00:11:29,583 --> 00:11:31,441
Why is this so long?

144
00:11:34,194 --> 00:11:37,074
Why is this so complicated?

145
00:11:40,008 --> 00:11:42,958
[Lee Hyeong Won's Autobiography]
[I've always wanted a new white outfit]

146
00:11:52,932 --> 00:11:55,080
I wrote plenty...

147
00:11:58,820 --> 00:12:00,298
All right.

148
00:12:00,298 --> 00:12:02,510
Maybe I should take a break.

149
00:12:02,510 --> 00:12:05,118
An autobiography...

150
00:12:05,118 --> 00:12:08,389
Right. Once you win gold,
publishers start calling like crazy.

151
00:12:08,389 --> 00:12:10,795
I never thought of that.

152
00:12:11,814 --> 00:12:14,463
But why would he go into hiding?

153
00:12:14,463 --> 00:12:17,590
If you're just playing dumb to avoid me,

154
00:12:17,590 --> 00:12:19,132
then let's stop.

155
00:12:20,991 --> 00:12:22,338
But...

156
00:12:30,292 --> 00:12:33,522
What if it isn't Hyeong Won...
then who's Chu Si Hwan?

157
00:12:34,205 --> 00:12:36,643
If you'd ever actually listened to me...

158
00:12:36,643 --> 00:12:39,050
you wouldn't be saying
Chu Si Hwan is Hyeong Won.

159
00:12:39,050 --> 00:12:41,571
So who is it?

160
00:12:49,513 --> 00:12:52,467
Ha Ru... please don't mess this up.

161
00:12:52,467 --> 00:12:54,447
- Just a moment.
- Yeah.

162
00:12:56,228 --> 00:12:57,748
Yoon Ha Ru!

163
00:12:58,528 --> 00:12:59,769
Where've you been?

164
00:12:59,769 --> 00:13:01,809
Oh, unnie.

165
00:13:02,805 --> 00:13:04,367
"Unnie?"

166
00:13:04,367 --> 00:13:07,152
You're impossible to read.

167
00:13:07,152 --> 00:13:08,636
Where's Ha Na?

168
00:13:09,499 --> 00:13:11,132
Ha Na?

169
00:13:12,339 --> 00:13:16,326
She's over there talking to Woo Jae.

170
00:13:16,326 --> 00:13:18,238
Just the two of them?

171
00:13:18,238 --> 00:13:19,597
How's it going?

172
00:13:19,597 --> 00:13:20,832
Are they okay?

173
00:13:20,832 --> 00:13:22,928
Hope they work things out.

174
00:13:22,928 --> 00:13:24,694
No idea.

175
00:13:28,888 --> 00:13:30,092
Babe.

176
00:13:30,092 --> 00:13:31,943
Don't you think...

177
00:13:31,943 --> 00:13:35,622
we should work on us too?

178
00:13:36,719 --> 00:13:39,563
Oh, yeah.

179
00:13:39,563 --> 00:13:43,398
About us...

180
00:13:43,398 --> 00:13:44,995
Hey! Guys!

181
00:13:44,995 --> 00:13:47,235
They're here.

182
00:13:54,251 --> 00:13:57,284
Did the talk go okay?

183
00:13:58,349 --> 00:14:00,388
Yeah, I guess.

184
00:14:01,941 --> 00:14:04,258
Woo Jae really came through for us.

185
00:14:04,258 --> 00:14:06,069
I'm proud of him.

186
00:14:06,069 --> 00:14:08,752
Thank you, Woo Jae.

187
00:14:08,752 --> 00:14:11,185
Thanks, Woo Jae.

188
00:14:11,185 --> 00:14:13,103
It's about Ha Ru.

189
00:14:13,103 --> 00:14:15,121
I'll do whatever I can to help.

190
00:14:15,121 --> 00:14:17,503
You're the best.

191
00:14:20,470 --> 00:14:21,959
Seok Min?

192
00:14:21,959 --> 00:14:23,085
Yes.

193
00:14:24,486 --> 00:14:28,019
- Yes, CEO Seo.
- Where's Director Chu now?

194
00:14:28,019 --> 00:14:29,512
One second.

195
00:14:31,132 --> 00:14:35,820
Oh, Director Chu Si Hwan
happens to be in Haesol too.

196
00:14:35,820 --> 00:14:37,973
I set up a meeting for today.

197
00:14:38,823 --> 00:14:40,747
Just come up a little farther...

198
00:14:40,747 --> 00:14:42,758
Can you see me?

199
00:14:42,758 --> 00:14:44,436
Over here!

200
00:14:44,436 --> 00:14:45,754
Hello.

201
00:14:45,754 --> 00:14:47,367
This way, please.

202
00:14:50,041 --> 00:14:52,237
He's here.

203
00:15:02,288 --> 00:15:06,585
Director Chu Si Hwan is... you?

204
00:15:07,245 --> 00:15:09,644
It's been a while, everyone.

205
00:15:13,146 --> 00:15:14,826
Woo Jae.

206
00:15:16,619 --> 00:15:18,241
Ha Na.

207
00:15:20,473 --> 00:15:22,668
I missed you a lot.

208
00:15:26,668 --> 00:15:31,044
What? You could've told me.

209
00:15:31,847 --> 00:15:36,726
I never would've guessed
Chu Si Hwan was your pen name.

210
00:15:37,728 --> 00:15:40,747
I didn't want to burden you
when you're already so busy.

211
00:15:40,747 --> 00:15:44,382
And I wanted the script to stand on its own.

212
00:15:44,382 --> 00:15:45,712
CEO Seo.

213
00:15:45,712 --> 00:15:47,983
You seriously...

214
00:15:50,367 --> 00:15:53,031
"Lost time..."

215
00:15:53,871 --> 00:15:57,029
Time-slip stories are everywhere.

216
00:15:57,029 --> 00:16:02,404
But our development team is
really excited about yours.

217
00:16:02,404 --> 00:16:06,293
It's a fantasy,
but the characters feel so real.

218
00:16:06,293 --> 00:16:07,921
They said it's incredibly immersive.

219
00:16:07,921 --> 00:16:09,354
Really?

220
00:16:11,281 --> 00:16:12,991
I just want...

221
00:16:12,991 --> 00:16:15,712
the characters in my films
to feel like they're truly alive.

222
00:16:15,712 --> 00:16:17,809
Beyond the words on the page...

223
00:16:17,809 --> 00:16:20,709
actually living and breathing.

224
00:16:23,079 --> 00:16:25,530
That's why I study real people

225
00:16:25,530 --> 00:16:29,215
and do a lot of research.

226
00:16:30,981 --> 00:16:33,274
What's he smiling at?

227
00:16:34,050 --> 00:16:35,398
I knew.

228
00:16:35,398 --> 00:16:38,784
You haven't changed a bit.

229
00:16:38,784 --> 00:16:40,166
Hey.

230
00:16:40,166 --> 00:16:42,717
Do you know how worried I was?

231
00:16:42,717 --> 00:16:45,797
You changed your number,
then disappeared on us...

232
00:16:45,797 --> 00:16:47,140
Sorry.

233
00:16:47,758 --> 00:16:49,481
The camcorder...

234
00:16:52,666 --> 00:16:55,725
How did you come up with the camcorder?

235
00:16:55,725 --> 00:16:57,687
I thought it was interesting.

236
00:17:00,695 --> 00:17:02,728
Oh, that...

237
00:17:03,328 --> 00:17:07,338
I figured you'd ask,
so I brought it to show you.

238
00:17:15,154 --> 00:17:16,308
Is this it?

239
00:17:16,308 --> 00:17:19,732
The key that unlocked your creative block?

240
00:17:19,732 --> 00:17:21,591
Yeah.

241
00:17:21,591 --> 00:17:25,977
I got it by chance
during a slump a few years ago.

242
00:17:25,977 --> 00:17:27,429
It made me wonder...

243
00:17:27,429 --> 00:17:31,013
what if I could go back into old videos?

244
00:17:31,013 --> 00:17:32,760
But...

245
00:17:32,760 --> 00:17:37,015
for the lead to really need to go back...

246
00:17:38,055 --> 00:17:43,121
I figured someone had to die.

247
00:17:43,856 --> 00:17:46,313
Someone they love.

248
00:17:46,313 --> 00:17:50,152
Someone they'd give their life for.

249
00:17:50,152 --> 00:17:54,342
Then they'd do anything to find a way back.

250
00:17:54,342 --> 00:17:55,912
Don't you think?

251
00:18:05,711 --> 00:18:06,867
Yoon Ha Na.

252
00:18:06,867 --> 00:18:08,780
I think this thing's broken.

253
00:18:08,780 --> 00:18:10,640
Hey, why did you...

254
00:18:19,592 --> 00:18:20,726
Hey.

255
00:18:20,726 --> 00:18:22,273
You okay?

256
00:18:23,213 --> 00:18:25,094
What's wrong?

257
00:18:32,278 --> 00:18:33,832
I'm so scared.

258
00:18:33,832 --> 00:18:37,312
What if we suddenly get thrown
into another future again?

259
00:18:37,976 --> 00:18:41,386
What if I can't see Woo Jae again?

260
00:18:41,386 --> 00:18:42,564
No.

261
00:18:42,564 --> 00:18:45,335
As long as we don't drop it, it should be okay.

262
00:18:45,335 --> 00:18:48,879
We know for sure how to get back
to the past where he is.

263
00:18:48,879 --> 00:18:52,249
"The past where he is?"

264
00:19:00,765 --> 00:19:05,186
Anyway, Jun Mo still has it.

265
00:19:06,916 --> 00:19:09,233
What did you two think?

266
00:19:09,233 --> 00:19:13,789
He really wants you two for the roles.

267
00:19:17,324 --> 00:19:20,234
- Maybe we should pass...
- Interesting.

268
00:19:22,264 --> 00:19:23,827
Really?

269
00:19:23,827 --> 00:19:26,011
- You liked it?
- Yeah.

270
00:19:26,011 --> 00:19:28,122
I've always liked your scripts.

271
00:19:28,122 --> 00:19:31,228
And you gave me this huge comeback project...

272
00:19:31,228 --> 00:19:35,094
You're still the only one who looks out for me.

273
00:19:35,094 --> 00:19:36,989
What the hell is he doing?

274
00:19:36,989 --> 00:19:38,886
So, Ha Na,

275
00:19:38,886 --> 00:19:40,229
you're in?

276
00:19:40,229 --> 00:19:41,358
Of course.

277
00:19:41,358 --> 00:19:43,030
I'd be honored to be in your film.

278
00:19:43,030 --> 00:19:44,607
Hey, Yoon Ha Ru...

279
00:19:45,429 --> 00:19:47,276
Yoon Ha Na!

280
00:19:48,648 --> 00:19:51,897
When are you thinking of shooting?

281
00:19:53,181 --> 00:19:58,501
We need to lock the cast first
before we set the schedule.

282
00:20:02,664 --> 00:20:04,210
Well...

283
00:20:04,829 --> 00:20:06,978
I'm afraid I can't do it.

284
00:20:09,546 --> 00:20:12,918
Why? You didn't like it?

285
00:20:12,918 --> 00:20:16,744
It gave me chills, sir.

286
00:20:19,410 --> 00:20:21,603
- "Chills?"
- Yes.

287
00:20:22,429 --> 00:20:25,562
Like someone stole a diary
and made it a script.

288
00:20:26,168 --> 00:20:28,531
And Eun Soo, the female lead...

289
00:20:29,128 --> 00:20:34,766
She acts like he's the love of her life,

290
00:20:34,766 --> 00:20:39,953
then dumps him for her own success.

291
00:20:40,657 --> 00:20:42,973
That's pretty realistic too.

292
00:20:42,973 --> 00:20:43,987
Well...

293
00:20:43,987 --> 00:20:47,220
If that's what you call hyperrealism,
I respect it.

294
00:20:47,220 --> 00:20:49,446
It's just not for me.

295
00:20:51,796 --> 00:20:53,247
Sorry.

296
00:20:53,247 --> 00:20:54,961
I'll get going.

297
00:21:05,551 --> 00:21:07,267
Sorry.

298
00:21:07,267 --> 00:21:10,033
Woo Jae's been a little on edge lately...

299
00:21:11,805 --> 00:21:12,925
Jun Mo.

300
00:21:12,925 --> 00:21:14,652
Let's have dinner.

301
00:21:14,652 --> 00:21:16,784
Today's just pre-shooting,
so we'll be done in no time.

302
00:21:16,784 --> 00:21:18,774
Let's catch up. It's been a while.

303
00:21:21,785 --> 00:21:23,749
- Shall we?
- Yeah.

304
00:21:23,749 --> 00:21:25,606
Dinner's on me.

305
00:21:25,606 --> 00:21:27,106
Great.

306
00:21:34,887 --> 00:21:36,880
Hey, Woo Jae.

307
00:21:40,648 --> 00:21:43,066
Can we talk for a second?

308
00:21:43,066 --> 00:21:46,110
If it's not urgent, let's talk after the shoot.

309
00:21:46,110 --> 00:21:48,004
I'm going to take a break.

310
00:21:51,021 --> 00:21:53,768
Just give him some time.

311
00:21:58,192 --> 00:22:01,585
[Yoon's Raw Fish Restaurant]

312
00:22:01,585 --> 00:22:04,655
It's so nice to drink together again.

313
00:22:04,655 --> 00:22:05,655
Right?

314
00:22:05,655 --> 00:22:08,364
I'm really glad to see you again, Jun Mo.

315
00:22:08,364 --> 00:22:10,244
Me too.

316
00:22:18,448 --> 00:22:20,227
I'm going to get some air.

317
00:22:20,227 --> 00:22:21,477
Want me to come with you?

318
00:22:21,477 --> 00:22:22,744
I'm good.

319
00:22:28,980 --> 00:22:30,725
Hey, back then...

320
00:22:30,725 --> 00:22:32,964
You know...

321
00:22:33,792 --> 00:22:36,722
after all the hell you went through
on "Silence of Paradise..."

322
00:22:36,722 --> 00:22:38,305
You remember?

323
00:22:39,999 --> 00:22:42,179
Yeah, right.

324
00:22:42,818 --> 00:22:45,970
I was so clueless back then.

325
00:22:45,970 --> 00:22:48,935
Still, those bastards...

326
00:22:48,935 --> 00:22:51,819
Once the investors came in, it was,
"Bring in an established director."

327
00:22:51,819 --> 00:22:54,136
"Replace Ha Na with Ha Hyun Ji."

328
00:22:54,136 --> 00:22:56,067
One ridiculous demand after another.

329
00:22:56,067 --> 00:22:57,967
Darn it.

330
00:22:57,967 --> 00:22:59,245
But...

331
00:22:59,245 --> 00:23:03,882
Jun Mo, you kept saying,
"Yoon Ha Na is the lead!"

332
00:23:03,882 --> 00:23:08,034
You went up against the production company
and the investors for her.

333
00:23:09,543 --> 00:23:11,349
Of course...

334
00:23:11,349 --> 00:23:14,306
You lost the rights
and walked away with nothing.

335
00:23:14,306 --> 00:23:15,678
Forget it.

336
00:23:15,678 --> 00:23:18,505
That's all in the past.

337
00:23:18,505 --> 00:23:21,291
What matters is what comes next.

338
00:23:22,685 --> 00:23:23,849
- Right.
- Cheers!

339
00:23:23,849 --> 00:23:27,022
- There you are. Let's have a toast!
- Cheers!

340
00:23:27,022 --> 00:23:30,457
Once you're done here,
keep the party going at our place.

341
00:23:30,457 --> 00:23:34,401
We've got plenty of snacks, so help yourselves.

342
00:23:34,401 --> 00:23:36,021
You stocked the fridge, right?

343
00:23:36,021 --> 00:23:38,796
Yeah. Plenty of soju and beer.

344
00:23:38,796 --> 00:23:41,849
I'll set out all the bedding,

345
00:23:41,849 --> 00:23:45,857
so if you hit your limit,
just crash right there.

346
00:23:45,857 --> 00:23:50,212
I'll take care of your hangover
tomorrow morning too. Okay?

347
00:23:50,212 --> 00:23:52,036
- You're the best!
- Thank you!

348
00:23:52,036 --> 00:23:53,332
Thank you!

349
00:23:55,009 --> 00:23:56,127
Babe.

350
00:23:56,127 --> 00:23:58,533
Is my face red?

351
00:23:59,690 --> 00:24:02,298
No, you look fine.

352
00:24:03,944 --> 00:24:05,904
I need the bathroom...

353
00:24:07,128 --> 00:24:08,573
CEO Seo.

354
00:24:08,573 --> 00:24:10,064
Yeah?

355
00:24:10,064 --> 00:24:12,747
I've got something on my mind.

356
00:24:12,747 --> 00:24:14,105
Something?

357
00:24:14,767 --> 00:24:18,151
I went on a blind date recently.

358
00:24:18,151 --> 00:24:21,572
- A blind date?
- Why hasn't she... called me?

359
00:24:21,572 --> 00:24:22,896
Dad, I...

360
00:24:22,896 --> 00:24:26,419
Why hasn't she called me?

361
00:24:26,419 --> 00:24:28,237
- Soo Hyuk.
- Yeah?

362
00:24:28,237 --> 00:24:30,085
What's with your hair?

363
00:24:30,085 --> 00:24:31,644
Well...

364
00:24:58,957 --> 00:25:01,038
Yoon Ha Ru!

365
00:25:01,038 --> 00:25:02,279
Are you out of your mind?

366
00:25:02,279 --> 00:25:03,903
You know how Woo Jae and I broke up,

367
00:25:03,903 --> 00:25:05,659
and you still said yes to that movie?

368
00:25:05,659 --> 00:25:08,812
"You're still the only one
who looks out for me?"

369
00:25:08,812 --> 00:25:10,519
Did you see Woo Jae's face?

370
00:25:10,519 --> 00:25:13,377
Because of you... I hurt him again.

371
00:25:13,377 --> 00:25:15,407
- It's okay.
- What's okay?

372
00:25:15,407 --> 00:25:17,532
Is it enough that you're okay?

373
00:25:17,532 --> 00:25:20,399
- Let's go back to 2017.
- What?

374
00:25:20,399 --> 00:25:23,972
Then none of this
would have happened to Woo Jae.

375
00:25:24,598 --> 00:25:27,175
The most important thing right now...

376
00:25:27,175 --> 00:25:28,667
is Yang Jun Mo.

377
00:25:28,667 --> 00:25:30,239
We need to learn more about him.

378
00:25:30,239 --> 00:25:32,947
Then we'll know what to prevent.

379
00:25:32,947 --> 00:25:34,743
What?

380
00:25:34,743 --> 00:25:38,193
You did that on purpose?

381
00:25:38,193 --> 00:25:39,644
This is Jun Mo's bag.

382
00:25:39,644 --> 00:25:41,897
There has to be something in here.

383
00:25:42,572 --> 00:25:44,294
Let's go home.

384
00:25:49,334 --> 00:25:51,159
That's why...

385
00:25:51,159 --> 00:25:54,668
Women are all like that.

386
00:25:55,439 --> 00:25:57,175
Exactly.

387
00:26:03,328 --> 00:26:05,334
You know...

388
00:26:05,334 --> 00:26:07,378
Since we're talking about relationships...

389
00:26:07,378 --> 00:26:08,609
Yeah?

390
00:26:10,527 --> 00:26:12,628
It's about a friend of mine.

391
00:26:14,199 --> 00:26:20,181
Her boyfriend suddenly
stopped wanting any affection.

392
00:26:21,248 --> 00:26:26,165
He freaks out whenever she gets close.

393
00:26:26,165 --> 00:26:28,089
Why would he do that?

394
00:26:28,089 --> 00:26:31,341
He's lost interest. Simple as that.

395
00:26:31,341 --> 00:26:33,580
How long have they been together?

396
00:26:35,319 --> 00:26:39,486
Eight or nine years, I think.

397
00:26:39,486 --> 00:26:42,797
That's plenty of time to get tired of someone.

398
00:26:42,797 --> 00:26:45,060
- Or maybe there's another woman.
- Hold on.

399
00:26:45,060 --> 00:26:48,264
- Right.
- Something smells fishy here.

400
00:26:48,264 --> 00:26:50,433
She might want to look into him.

401
00:26:50,433 --> 00:26:52,182
No, no. Forget that.

402
00:26:52,182 --> 00:26:56,550
Why waste time? She should just move on...

403
00:26:58,391 --> 00:27:02,097
How can love just change like that?

404
00:27:04,950 --> 00:27:06,471
1-2-3-4?

405
00:27:08,250 --> 00:27:10,389
That was never going to work.

406
00:27:10,389 --> 00:27:12,366
Yang Jun Mo's birthday?

407
00:27:12,366 --> 00:27:13,503
October 28.

408
00:27:13,503 --> 00:27:15,245
October 28...

409
00:27:19,178 --> 00:27:22,466
How are we supposed to guess all these?

410
00:27:22,466 --> 00:27:24,398
Anything else?

411
00:27:48,126 --> 00:27:49,137
[My Little Canary]

412
00:27:49,137 --> 00:27:51,229
What is this?

413
00:28:00,432 --> 00:28:02,199
"Canary?"

414
00:28:15,586 --> 00:28:16,987
It worked!

415
00:28:20,945 --> 00:28:22,210
CEO Seo, here...

416
00:28:22,210 --> 00:28:23,380
A tissue...

417
00:28:23,380 --> 00:28:25,853
She's drunk.

418
00:28:27,064 --> 00:28:28,467
Oh, my...

419
00:28:28,467 --> 00:28:30,506
Be careful.

420
00:28:32,839 --> 00:28:34,990
Where are Ha Na and Ha Ru?

421
00:28:34,990 --> 00:28:37,394
They were looking for their father earlier.

422
00:28:37,394 --> 00:28:38,911
- Yeah?
- Guys.

423
00:28:38,911 --> 00:28:40,931
Try this. It's good.

424
00:28:40,931 --> 00:28:42,783
Go on, eat.

425
00:28:43,599 --> 00:28:45,606
Thanks.

426
00:28:51,762 --> 00:28:53,087
Sir.

427
00:28:53,087 --> 00:28:54,807
- Yes, Director Yang?
- Well...

428
00:28:54,807 --> 00:28:57,913
It's been a while since I drank.
It's hitting me fast.

429
00:28:57,913 --> 00:29:01,450
I think I'll head in
and sleep for about 30 minutes.

430
00:29:01,450 --> 00:29:04,057
- You're not trying to ditch us, are you?
- Of course not.

431
00:29:04,057 --> 00:29:06,689
30 minutes, then you're back
for round two. Deal?

432
00:29:06,689 --> 00:29:09,658
- Of course.
- Oh, right. The gate key...

433
00:29:11,429 --> 00:29:12,819
- Thanks.
- Follow me.

434
00:29:12,819 --> 00:29:14,011
Okay.

435
00:29:14,011 --> 00:29:16,828
Jun Mo, just take a quick nap.
We've still got round two.

436
00:29:16,828 --> 00:29:19,177
- See you later.
- See you.

437
00:29:19,934 --> 00:29:22,226
- Round two!
- Not yet.

438
00:29:22,226 --> 00:29:23,822
- Hey, calm down.
- Round two...

439
00:30:10,099 --> 00:30:11,725
[Canary]

440
00:30:13,550 --> 00:30:14,625
[My Little Canary]

441
00:30:20,037 --> 00:30:21,659
I finally found it.

442
00:30:21,659 --> 00:30:24,026
My little canary.

443
00:30:24,955 --> 00:30:27,892
She stole my soul at first sight.

444
00:30:27,892 --> 00:30:30,679
We're each other's salvation.

445
00:30:30,679 --> 00:30:34,719
What the hell is this?

446
00:30:34,719 --> 00:30:37,171
This guy's completely insane.

447
00:30:37,171 --> 00:30:41,925
I'm the only sanctuary
that can protect her fragile life

448
00:30:41,925 --> 00:30:43,580
from this cruel world.

449
00:30:43,580 --> 00:30:47,188
You should only breathe inside my cage.

450
00:30:48,493 --> 00:30:54,144
My canary dared to leave my cage.

451
00:30:54,144 --> 00:30:57,425
Even if I have to stop her from breathing...
I'll bring her back.

452
00:30:57,425 --> 00:31:01,943
I'll become the only shelter you have...

453
00:31:01,943 --> 00:31:05,327
so you'll never leave my cage again.

454
00:31:06,118 --> 00:31:09,494
Tonight, I'm reminded of an artist
who turned his muse into a stuffed doll,

455
00:31:09,494 --> 00:31:13,495
cut off its head, and held a funeral for it.

456
00:31:16,249 --> 00:31:18,410
Only your death...

457
00:31:20,003 --> 00:31:24,571
can complete the most beautiful,
perfect sanctuary I could ever create.

458
00:32:50,366 --> 00:32:51,851
Who's that?

459
00:32:51,851 --> 00:32:54,431
Mom and Dad wouldn't be home yet.

460
00:32:55,362 --> 00:32:56,874
What is this...

461
00:33:39,636 --> 00:33:41,589
Ha Na. Are you in there?

462
00:33:42,256 --> 00:33:43,426
Yang Jun Mo?

463
00:33:43,426 --> 00:33:44,733
What do we do?

464
00:33:44,733 --> 00:33:47,917
Want me to knock him out?

465
00:33:48,652 --> 00:33:51,166
Let's just get out of here first.

466
00:33:52,741 --> 00:33:54,226
You got the camcorder, right?

467
00:33:57,577 --> 00:33:58,900
Yeah.

468
00:34:02,910 --> 00:34:05,347
Open the door, Ha Na.

469
00:34:05,347 --> 00:34:07,069
It's me, Jun Mo.

470
00:34:36,607 --> 00:34:37,617
Too obvious.

471
00:34:37,617 --> 00:34:39,517
Ha Na!

472
00:34:39,517 --> 00:34:41,552
Found the key.

473
00:34:42,263 --> 00:34:44,464
I'll open it for you.

474
00:35:42,389 --> 00:35:43,883
Now!

475
00:35:54,731 --> 00:35:56,135
You saw it.

476
00:36:03,747 --> 00:36:05,165
Be careful.

477
00:37:19,531 --> 00:37:20,978
No!

478
00:37:23,648 --> 00:37:25,035
Hurry!

479
00:38:15,509 --> 00:38:17,535
That smell...

480
00:38:18,743 --> 00:38:23,671
[October 17, 2017]
[Woo Jae's 25th Birthday]

481
00:38:23,671 --> 00:38:26,716
The birthday cake
I totally ruined for Woo Jae...

482
00:38:51,347 --> 00:38:53,190
Did you wait up for me?

483
00:39:10,814 --> 00:39:13,304
I'm never...

484
00:39:13,304 --> 00:39:16,337
ever letting you go again.

485
00:39:16,337 --> 00:39:19,130
What are you talking about?

486
00:39:25,339 --> 00:39:26,736
But...

487
00:39:26,736 --> 00:39:29,210
what's that smell?

488
00:39:30,579 --> 00:39:34,086
Oh, I burned the cake.

489
00:39:35,589 --> 00:39:38,240
But it's okay. Ha Ru's bringing one.

490
00:39:38,240 --> 00:39:39,641
Probably...

491
00:39:42,333 --> 00:39:45,365
Happy birthday, Jung Woo Jae.

492
00:39:51,836 --> 00:39:53,488
Thanks.

493
00:39:54,243 --> 00:39:56,076
I'm so happy.

494
00:40:01,735 --> 00:40:03,899
Hey. Enough already.

495
00:40:03,899 --> 00:40:05,823
Can we go inside now?

496
00:40:05,823 --> 00:40:07,085
Jeez.

497
00:40:07,085 --> 00:40:12,013
Watching my best friend date my twin sister...

498
00:40:12,013 --> 00:40:13,047
Come on.

499
00:40:13,047 --> 00:40:15,978
This is still Ye Rang Entertainment housing.

500
00:40:15,978 --> 00:40:18,315
We've even got a new manager moving in today.

501
00:40:18,315 --> 00:40:21,210
Please tone down the PDA a little.

502
00:40:21,210 --> 00:40:23,576
Did that scare you?

503
00:40:23,576 --> 00:40:25,048
I'm fine!

504
00:40:25,048 --> 00:40:26,393
He's the new guy.

505
00:40:26,393 --> 00:40:27,520
Hello.

506
00:40:27,520 --> 00:40:30,590
I'm Gwak Seong Min. I just joined the team.

507
00:40:30,590 --> 00:40:32,064
I'll do my best.

508
00:40:32,064 --> 00:40:33,690
Ta-da!

509
00:40:34,843 --> 00:40:36,213
Ta-da.

510
00:40:38,636 --> 00:40:46,123
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

511
00:40:46,123 --> 00:40:49,616
♪ Dear Jung Woo Jae ♪

512
00:40:49,616 --> 00:40:53,146
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

513
00:40:53,146 --> 00:40:55,807
- Make a wish!
- Make a wish.

514
00:41:00,820 --> 00:41:02,902
What did you wish for?

515
00:41:02,902 --> 00:41:04,906
- It's a secret.
- Yeah?

516
00:41:04,906 --> 00:41:07,372
- Can you take a picture for us?
- Sure.

517
00:41:10,308 --> 00:41:12,192
I'll take it.

518
00:41:12,192 --> 00:41:14,678
One, two, three!

519
00:41:15,359 --> 00:41:16,642
One more.

520
00:41:16,642 --> 00:41:19,083
One, two, three!

521
00:41:19,083 --> 00:41:21,320
- Hey. Let's take one together.
- Come on.

522
00:41:21,320 --> 00:41:23,336
- Let's all take one.
- Should I?

523
00:41:24,283 --> 00:41:25,500
All right.

524
00:41:25,500 --> 00:41:26,533
Everyone, squeeze in.

525
00:41:26,533 --> 00:41:28,869
One, two, three!

526
00:41:31,974 --> 00:41:33,520
Get over here!

527
00:41:36,103 --> 00:41:37,652
Keep it clean!

528
00:41:42,120 --> 00:41:43,764
A, B, B!

529
00:41:43,764 --> 00:41:45,353
- I'll hit you.
- Okay.

530
00:41:47,373 --> 00:41:48,930
That hurts!

531
00:41:48,930 --> 00:41:51,053
Go easy on me!

532
00:41:54,571 --> 00:41:56,431
A, B, A!

533
00:42:00,355 --> 00:42:02,354
A, B, B!

534
00:42:15,661 --> 00:42:17,955
Should we report that psycho to the police?

535
00:42:17,955 --> 00:42:20,678
And tell them what?

536
00:42:20,678 --> 00:42:24,027
- What?
- That nine years from now, in 2026,

537
00:42:24,027 --> 00:42:26,711
Jun Mo's going to come after us with a knife...

538
00:42:26,711 --> 00:42:29,424
Report him for attempted murder in the future?

539
00:42:31,141 --> 00:42:32,704
Then what about the laptop?

540
00:42:32,704 --> 00:42:34,330
He's been writing that stuff since 2012.

541
00:42:34,330 --> 00:42:37,834
All that "my little canary" crap.

542
00:42:37,834 --> 00:42:39,738
But my name wasn't in it.

543
00:42:39,738 --> 00:42:42,804
It's just some symbolic metaphor
he wrote for himself.

544
00:42:45,285 --> 00:42:48,243
Right now, Jun Mo hasn't done anything.

545
00:42:48,243 --> 00:42:51,321
He's just an innocent film student

546
00:42:51,321 --> 00:42:55,682
with a twisted imagination
who wrote some creepy stuff on his laptop.

547
00:42:55,682 --> 00:42:58,482
Then what do we do?

548
00:43:00,176 --> 00:43:03,633
I'm not going to be an actress.

549
00:43:03,633 --> 00:43:05,249
Sorry?

550
00:43:05,249 --> 00:43:06,377
Hey.

551
00:43:06,377 --> 00:43:08,334
Are you sure?

552
00:43:08,334 --> 00:43:10,171
Yeah.

553
00:43:10,171 --> 00:43:12,805
Jun Mo is the one who tried to kill me.

554
00:43:12,805 --> 00:43:15,604
And Woo Jae got hurt again trying to save me...

555
00:43:15,604 --> 00:43:19,224
I think this is the only way
to avoid that fate.

556
00:43:19,224 --> 00:43:21,194
I have to quit.

557
00:43:21,947 --> 00:43:23,304
But...

558
00:43:23,304 --> 00:43:27,391
Can you really live without being an actress?

559
00:43:27,391 --> 00:43:29,551
Why couldn't I?

560
00:43:29,551 --> 00:43:32,018
You gave up judo too.

561
00:43:32,018 --> 00:43:33,764
Because of me.

562
00:43:33,764 --> 00:43:35,761
Come on. That's different.

563
00:43:35,761 --> 00:43:37,695
I'm fine.

564
00:43:37,695 --> 00:43:40,028
In this life...

565
00:43:40,028 --> 00:43:43,200
as long as Woo Jae doesn't get hurt
because of me.

566
00:43:44,103 --> 00:43:45,867
That's all I need.

567
00:43:55,722 --> 00:43:57,383
[Senior Yang Jun Mo, Class 50]

568
00:44:01,841 --> 00:44:03,353
Hello?

569
00:44:04,019 --> 00:44:07,252
Oh, Ha Na. I was actually about to call you.

570
00:44:07,252 --> 00:44:08,929
Yeah? Perfect.

571
00:44:08,929 --> 00:44:12,518
The revised draft of my new film is ready.

572
00:44:12,518 --> 00:44:13,675
Jun Mo,

573
00:44:13,675 --> 00:44:15,700
want to meet tomorrow?

574
00:44:15,700 --> 00:44:17,425
Sure.

575
00:44:17,425 --> 00:44:20,403
Okay. See you there tomorrow.

576
00:44:23,934 --> 00:44:25,396
Ha Na.

577
00:44:28,126 --> 00:44:29,579
Yes?

578
00:44:30,868 --> 00:44:32,491
What are you doing?

579
00:44:32,491 --> 00:44:34,181
I have to go now.

580
00:44:35,798 --> 00:44:37,735
Yeah. Let's all head out.

581
00:44:37,735 --> 00:44:39,419
Let's go.

582
00:44:39,419 --> 00:44:40,658
Come on, let's go.

583
00:44:42,140 --> 00:44:44,212
[Happy Home]

584
00:44:46,951 --> 00:44:48,409
I wish I could stay longer...

585
00:44:48,409 --> 00:44:50,123
but I've got an early schedule tomorrow.

586
00:44:50,123 --> 00:44:51,340
Don't worry about us.

587
00:44:51,340 --> 00:44:53,500
Go get some sleep.

588
00:44:53,500 --> 00:44:55,564
Happy birthday, Jung Woo Jae.

589
00:44:55,564 --> 00:44:57,091
Thanks.

590
00:44:57,091 --> 00:44:58,731
- I'll get going, Ha Na.
- Okay.

591
00:44:58,731 --> 00:45:00,172
Get home safe.

592
00:45:09,604 --> 00:45:11,534
This is my last chance.

593
00:45:11,534 --> 00:45:14,658
Woo Jae, you and everything you care about...

594
00:45:14,658 --> 00:45:16,671
I'll protect it all.

595
00:45:16,671 --> 00:45:20,344
I'll risk everything to keep you safe.

596
00:45:37,630 --> 00:45:39,256
Ha Na.

597
00:45:40,278 --> 00:45:42,117
Did you wait long?

598
00:45:42,117 --> 00:45:44,120
I just got here too.

599
00:45:53,572 --> 00:45:54,910
Ta-da!

600
00:45:54,910 --> 00:45:58,403
[Silence of Paradise]
Silence of Paradise... You remember?

601
00:45:58,403 --> 00:46:01,206
Once the investors came in, it was,
"Bring in an established director."

602
00:46:01,206 --> 00:46:03,155
"Replace Ha Na with Ha Hyun Ji."

603
00:46:03,155 --> 00:46:04,856
One ridiculous demand after another.

604
00:46:04,856 --> 00:46:06,133
But...

605
00:46:06,133 --> 00:46:10,644
Jun Mo, you kept saying,
"Yoon Ha Na is the lead!"

606
00:46:10,644 --> 00:46:14,276
You went up against the production company
and the investors for her.

607
00:46:14,276 --> 00:46:15,727
Of course...

608
00:46:15,727 --> 00:46:20,099
You lost the rights
and walked away with nothing.

609
00:46:22,358 --> 00:46:25,156
It's still a graduation film,

610
00:46:25,156 --> 00:46:28,335
but the producer sent it around
to a few agencies.

611
00:46:28,335 --> 00:46:29,799
You know Ha Hyun Ji, right?

612
00:46:29,799 --> 00:46:32,529
She went to Cannes last year
with "Gyeongseong Lady."

613
00:46:32,529 --> 00:46:34,043
Yeah. I know.

614
00:46:34,043 --> 00:46:35,587
Her agency wanted a meeting.

615
00:46:35,587 --> 00:46:36,931
I turned them down.

616
00:46:36,931 --> 00:46:41,022
This film has to be you.

617
00:46:41,849 --> 00:46:44,729
Our seniors made Cannes with graduation films.

618
00:46:44,729 --> 00:46:47,847
The producers already have big plans
for my script.

619
00:46:47,847 --> 00:46:50,684
They're even talking
about a full theatrical release.

620
00:46:50,684 --> 00:46:51,957
Cannes?

621
00:46:51,957 --> 00:46:54,248
I think it's your turn, Ha Na.

622
00:46:57,066 --> 00:46:59,198
- Jun Mo...
- Yes?

623
00:47:00,486 --> 00:47:02,327
I can't do this.

624
00:47:03,519 --> 00:47:04,841
I'm sorry.

625
00:47:06,578 --> 00:47:07,899
What?

626
00:47:10,479 --> 00:47:12,176
What are you talking about?

627
00:47:12,176 --> 00:47:15,552
- At least read it first...
- I...

628
00:47:15,552 --> 00:47:17,672
I'm quitting acting.

629
00:47:18,626 --> 00:47:19,662
What?

630
00:47:19,662 --> 00:47:23,206
I'm done being an actress.

631
00:47:23,206 --> 00:47:24,836
I'll find something else.

632
00:47:24,836 --> 00:47:26,115
Why?

633
00:47:28,877 --> 00:47:31,181
Hey, Ha Na.

634
00:47:31,181 --> 00:47:32,478
You're still a rookie.

635
00:47:32,478 --> 00:47:34,217
Why give up already?

636
00:47:34,217 --> 00:47:36,118
I'm not giving up.

637
00:47:36,118 --> 00:47:38,458
I just don't want to do it anymore.

638
00:47:39,487 --> 00:47:41,190
Jun Mo.

639
00:47:41,190 --> 00:47:44,290
This is a huge opportunity for you.

640
00:47:44,290 --> 00:47:47,205
So hold on to Ha Hyun Ji.

641
00:47:47,951 --> 00:47:51,141
I respect how strongly
you believe in your work.

642
00:47:51,141 --> 00:47:52,667
But...

643
00:47:52,667 --> 00:47:54,411
you're a professional now.

644
00:47:54,411 --> 00:47:56,752
Maybe it's okay to compromise sometimes.

645
00:47:56,752 --> 00:48:03,398
I just don't want you to lose your film.

646
00:48:11,209 --> 00:48:12,629
I see.

647
00:48:16,481 --> 00:48:18,118
Well, then...

648
00:48:18,118 --> 00:48:19,942
It can't be helped.

649
00:48:21,501 --> 00:48:23,284
I'm sorry, Jun Mo.

650
00:48:32,288 --> 00:48:33,651
Ha Na.

651
00:48:35,988 --> 00:48:39,021
Could you do me one favor?

652
00:48:41,588 --> 00:48:43,211
- Good work!
- Good work!

653
00:48:43,211 --> 00:48:45,112
Are you heading home?

654
00:48:45,893 --> 00:48:48,263
Drop me off at the shared house.

655
00:48:48,263 --> 00:48:49,793
What?

656
00:48:49,793 --> 00:48:51,349
You saw her yesterday.

657
00:48:51,349 --> 00:48:53,074
Miss her that much?

658
00:48:53,074 --> 00:48:55,192
Like her that much?

659
00:48:55,810 --> 00:48:58,029
I'll get you there safely.

660
00:48:58,710 --> 00:49:00,387
You know what Professor Min is like.

661
00:49:00,387 --> 00:49:02,602
She's as commercial as they come.

662
00:49:02,602 --> 00:49:07,188
She's probably dying to tear my script apart.

663
00:49:07,188 --> 00:49:09,941
I can't handle her alone.

664
00:49:10,735 --> 00:49:12,233
Okay...

665
00:49:15,005 --> 00:49:16,476
Darn it.

666
00:49:16,476 --> 00:49:19,452
Where are they going all of a sudden?

667
00:49:29,089 --> 00:49:32,279
By the way, Ha Na.

668
00:49:32,279 --> 00:49:33,326
Yeah?

669
00:49:33,326 --> 00:49:34,591
Until last week...

670
00:49:34,591 --> 00:49:36,663
No, even two days ago...

671
00:49:36,663 --> 00:49:38,770
you said you'd do it.

672
00:49:38,770 --> 00:49:40,970
You said you were grateful.

673
00:49:42,357 --> 00:49:43,524
Yeah.

674
00:49:43,524 --> 00:49:44,744
I did.

675
00:49:44,744 --> 00:49:47,437
And now, you're quitting acting?

676
00:50:14,785 --> 00:50:16,089
Jun Mo.

677
00:50:16,089 --> 00:50:17,266
Slow down.

678
00:50:17,266 --> 00:50:18,840
I'm scared...

679
00:50:19,473 --> 00:50:21,322
What's there to be scared of?

680
00:50:21,322 --> 00:50:23,551
I feel like we're going to crash.

681
00:51:20,822 --> 00:51:23,484
That psycho...

682
00:51:24,714 --> 00:51:27,692
Please. What's gotten into you?

683
00:51:33,260 --> 00:51:34,669
Ha Na.

684
00:51:40,849 --> 00:51:43,353
She didn't say she was going anywhere...

685
00:51:43,353 --> 00:51:44,835
Where did she go?

686
00:51:51,379 --> 00:51:52,379
[Naa]

687
00:52:09,463 --> 00:52:11,166
I'm just going to the bathroom.

688
00:52:40,641 --> 00:52:42,781
What are you looking for?

689
00:52:45,561 --> 00:52:47,086
I...

690
00:52:47,086 --> 00:52:49,531
I think I lost my phone.

691
00:52:49,531 --> 00:52:51,309
That's too bad.

692
00:52:51,309 --> 00:52:52,541
But Ha Na.

693
00:52:52,541 --> 00:52:54,137
Yeah?

694
00:52:54,137 --> 00:52:55,486
Why...

695
00:52:57,971 --> 00:53:00,266
Why are you quitting acting?

696
00:53:01,758 --> 00:53:03,301
Why?

697
00:53:03,301 --> 00:53:04,582
Huh?

698
00:53:05,237 --> 00:53:06,562
Why?

699
00:53:06,562 --> 00:53:08,799
Something's changing...

700
00:53:08,799 --> 00:53:11,375
I've never seen him like this before.

701
00:53:12,490 --> 00:53:14,317
Hey.

702
00:53:14,317 --> 00:53:15,940
Why are you looking at me like that?

703
00:53:15,940 --> 00:53:17,714
Is it because of me?

704
00:53:17,714 --> 00:53:19,990
Because I changed the past?

705
00:53:20,706 --> 00:53:23,706
I'm just curious.

706
00:53:23,706 --> 00:53:26,256
Why would you quit acting?

707
00:53:26,256 --> 00:53:27,788
Why...

708
00:53:28,422 --> 00:53:29,954
Jun Mo.

709
00:53:37,782 --> 00:53:41,382
The person you are calling is unavailable...

710
00:53:50,912 --> 00:53:52,578
[Beast: Answer me]

711
00:53:56,788 --> 00:53:57,958
Yoon Ha Na.

712
00:53:57,958 --> 00:53:59,365
Check your messages.

713
00:53:59,365 --> 00:54:00,682
Why are you in that bastard's car?

714
00:54:00,682 --> 00:54:02,242
Where are you going? I lost you.

715
00:54:02,242 --> 00:54:03,380
Pick up.

716
00:54:03,380 --> 00:54:05,045
Yoon Ha Na!

717
00:54:05,045 --> 00:54:06,795
Pick up already.

718
00:54:06,795 --> 00:54:09,022
What the hell...

719
00:54:09,022 --> 00:54:10,739
is going on?

720
00:54:10,739 --> 00:54:12,035
Hang in there.

721
00:54:12,035 --> 00:54:14,402
I'm going home right now
to smash the camcorder.

722
00:54:14,402 --> 00:54:16,094
"The camcorder?"

723
00:54:23,689 --> 00:54:25,179
Ha Na.

724
00:54:25,179 --> 00:54:26,632
Yeah.

725
00:54:58,592 --> 00:55:00,679
What is this?

726
00:55:03,158 --> 00:55:06,125
"2026?"

727
00:55:08,767 --> 00:55:11,270
- Jun Mo.
- Yeah, Ha Na...

728
00:55:11,270 --> 00:55:12,629
Why?

729
00:55:14,567 --> 00:55:15,906
Why?

730
00:55:16,522 --> 00:55:18,035
Why!

731
00:55:25,219 --> 00:55:27,325
I'm asking you.

732
00:55:29,204 --> 00:55:30,491
Why?

733
00:55:31,475 --> 00:55:33,941
In the future you just came back from...

734
00:55:37,300 --> 00:55:39,548
Did I kill you or something?

735
00:56:21,604 --> 00:56:23,121
It started the same way before.

736
00:56:23,121 --> 00:56:27,333
From now on,
every trace he leaves is evidence for us.

737
00:56:27,333 --> 00:56:28,946
He'll show up again, right?

738
00:56:28,946 --> 00:56:30,438
I kept seeing it...

739
00:56:30,438 --> 00:56:32,471
That creepy look in his eyes.

740
00:56:34,011 --> 00:56:38,028
In the past, they'd give up everything for you.

741
00:56:38,028 --> 00:56:41,012
You and I may be in different situations...

742
00:56:41,012 --> 00:56:43,415
but we want the same thing.

743
00:56:43,415 --> 00:56:45,948
What do you want me to do?

744
00:56:45,948 --> 00:56:48,058
Let's get rid of them.

745
00:56:48,058 --> 00:56:50,406
I'll protect the past.
